 married to a Maldivian) is a 'temporary resident' taxed only on Maldivian-source income, so a foreign family's foreign portfolio would be untaxed. No wealth, inheritance or gift tax. Long-term residence for wealthy foreigners is hard to obtain.","regimes":[{"id":"standard","name":"Maldives tax residence (full resident)","type":"standard","description":"Worldwide taxation at up to 15% (applies to Maldivians and foreigners married to Maldivians).","eligible_citizenships":["EU","US","OTHER"],"eligibility":"Permanent home in the Maldives or 183+ days in a 12-month period, and not a temporary resident.","duration_years":null,"requires_qualifying_activity":false,"duration_note":"","lump_sum":null,"structure":null,"capital_gains":{"status":"researched","basis":"law_in_force","summary":"Capital gains are part of taxable income and taxed at the individual progressive rates (top 15% above MVR 2.4M) (Income Tax Act 25/2019, ss. 3 and 7). Residents are taxed on worldwide income (s. 10(a)).","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Income Tax Act: Overview & Impact (Jan 2020)","url":"https://www.ctlstrategies.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/20200106_Income-Tax-Act_Overview-Impact.pdf","publisher":"CTL Strategies (Maldives law firm)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Maldives: Business environment - taxes","url":"https://www.lloydsbanktrade.com/en/market-potential/maldives/taxes","publisher":"Lloyds Bank Trade (Export Entreprises)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"}],"verified_on":"2026-10-15","confidence":"medium","verification":"partially_verified","open_questions":["Lloyds Bank Trade states 'no capital gains tax is levied', contradicting CTL's reading of the Act; the Act itself (MIRA site blocks automated access) was not read.","Individual rate brackets after any 2024-2026 amendments were not verified (Lloyds lists the same brackets as '2023 brackets')."],"headline_rate":0.15,"rates":{"listed_securities_domestic":0.15,"listed_securities_foreign":0.15,"private_business_sale":0.15,"real_estate_local":0.15,"real_estate_foreign":0.15},"rate_basis":"Top marginal rate 15% applies above MVR 2.4M (~EUR 135k); a large gain is taxed at about 15%.","professional_trader":"","holding_period_rules":"","foreign_assets":"Full residents: worldwide, with a foreign tax credit (s. 72) capped at the Maldivian tax."},"dividends":{"status":"researched","basis":"law_in_force","summary":"Dividends received by a resident from a resident company are exempt (s. 12). Foreign dividends of a full resident are taxable at progressive rates up to 15%, with a foreign tax credit.","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Income Tax Act: Overview & Impact (Jan 2020)","url":"https://www.ctlstrategies.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/20200106_Income-Tax-Act_Overview-Impact.pdf","publisher":"CTL Strategies (Maldives law firm)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Maldives: Business environment - taxes","url":"https://www.lloydsbanktrade.com/en/market-potential/maldives/taxes","publisher":"Lloyds Bank Trade (Export Entreprises)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"}],"verified_on":"2026-10-15","confidence":"medium","verification":"partially_verified","open_questions":[],"headline_rate":0.15,"domestic_rate":0.0,"foreign_gross_rate":0.15,"foreign_tax_credit":"credit","credit_cap":null,"rate_basis":"Domestic 0 (exempt); foreign at the 15% top marginal rate.","withholding_outbound":"10% non-resident WHT on dividends (s. 55).","treaty_network":"Very small (a handful of treaties; not verified).","holding_company_notes":""},"wealth_tax":{"status":"researched","basis":"law_in_force","summary":"No net wealth tax.","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Maldives: Business environment - taxes","url":"https://www.lloydsbanktrade.com/en/market-potential/maldives/taxes","publisher":"Lloyds Bank Trade (Export Entreprises)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Income Tax Act: Overview & Impact (Jan 2020)","url":"https://www.ctlstrategies.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/20200106_Income-Tax-Act_Overview-Impact.pdf","publisher":"CTL Strategies (Maldives law firm)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"}],"verified_on":"2026-10-15","confidence":"medium","verification":"partially_verified","open_questions":[],"type":"none","components":[],"income_cap":null,"starts_after_years":null,"thresholds_indexed":false,"property_tax_note":"No recurring property tax on individuals was found. Foreigners cannot own freehold land (leasehold only)."},"inheritance":{"status":"researched","basis":"none","summary":"No inheritance, estate or gift tax. Gifts are exempt income subject to a de minimis rule and conditions (s. 12).","exemptions_thresholds":"","eligibility_conditions":"","regional_differences":"","important_exceptions":"Succession, not tax, is the issue: personal status law based on Sharia governs the estates of Muslims (fixed shares; a son typically takes twice a daughter's share; at most one third freely disposable by will to non-heirs). How estates of non-Muslim foreigners are handled (law of nationality, own religious rules, or Sharia by default) was not verified here; non-Muslim families should take local legal advice.","tax_year":"2026","sources":[{"title":"Income Tax Act: Overview & Impact (Jan 2020)","url":"https://www.ctlstrategies.com/wp-content/uploads/2020/01/20200106_Income-Tax-Act_Overview-Impact.pdf","publisher":"CTL Strategies (Maldives law firm)","kind":"professional","accessed":"2026-10-15"},{"title":"Maldives: Business environment - taxes","url":"https://www.lloydsbanktrade.com/en/market-potential/maldives/taxes","publisher":"Lloyds Bank Trade (Export 